      "username": "shaileshsaini",
      "name": "Shailesh",
      "created_at": "2026-01-07T06:45:26.837Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello,</p>\n<p>Please follow the steps below to send emails to multiple recipients at once:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>First, create an Email Group / Contact List.</strong><br>\nAdd or import all the required email addresses into this Email Group.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Next, go to the Email Campaign module</strong> and create a new Email Campaign.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>In the Email Campaign:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Enter the <strong>Campaign Name</strong> (Also set the Campaign Schedules)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Select <strong>Campaign Type</strong> as <em>Email Group</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Choose the <strong>Email Group</strong> that you created earlier</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>After verifying all the details, <strong>save</strong> the campaign and use <strong>Send Now</strong> or <strong>Schedule</strong> to send the emails.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Please try this approach — it should help you send emails to all recipients in one go.</p>\n<p>Thank you.</p>",
